  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models clearly dominate (0.485–0.520) over image-only (0.208), and scvi_n200 is the best RNA encoder tested (0.520 vs 0.485 for pca_n2000). The critical open question is whether multiprofile representation improves over singleprofile, since this choice gates a large portion of the remaining search space. config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) is the most direct extension of the best-performing config_004, isolating the effect of multiprofile + simple aggregation while holding the RNA encoder fixed. If multiprofile helps, it justifies investing further in aggregation variants and multimodal multiprofile configs; if it does not, we can deprioritize the entire multiprofile branch and focus budget on encoder selection or fusion strategy. This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice under the limited budget."
}

